  26:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****                   ##### How to use this driver #####
  27:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****   ==============================================================================
  28:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  29:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  30:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     The SAI HAL driver can be used as follows:
  31:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  32:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     (#) Declare a SAI_HandleTypeDef handle structure (eg. SAI_HandleTypeDef hsai).
  33:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     (#) Initialize the SAI low level resources by implementing the HAL_SAI_MspInit() API:
  34:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) Enable the SAI interface clock.
  35:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) SAI pins configuration:
  36:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Enable the clock for the SAI GPIOs.
  37:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure these SAI pins as alternate function pull-up.
  38:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process (HAL_SAI_Transmit_IT()
  39:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****              and HAL_SAI_Receive_IT() APIs):
  40:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure the SAI interrupt priority.
  41:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Enable the NVIC SAI IRQ handle.
  42:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  43:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) DMA Configuration if you need to use DMA process (HAL_SAI_Transmit_DMA()
  44:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****              and HAL_SAI_Receive_DMA() APIs):
  45:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Declare a DMA handle structure for the Tx/Rx stream.
  46:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Enable the DMAx interface clock.
  47:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure the declared DMA handle structure with the required Tx/Rx parameters.
  48:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure the DMA Tx/Rx Stream.
  49:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Associate the initialized DMA handle to the SAI DMA Tx/Rx handle.
  50:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure the priority and enable the NVIC for the transfer complete interrupt on
  51:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****                 DMA Tx/Rx Stream.
  52:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  53:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     (#) The initialization can be done by two ways
  54:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) Expert mode : Initialize the structures Init, FrameInit and SlotInit and call HAL_SAI_
  55:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) Simplified mode : Initialize the high part of Init Structure and call HAL_SAI_InitProt
  56:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  57:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  58:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) The specific SAI interrupts (FIFO request and Overrun underrun interrupt)
  59:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         will be managed using the macros __HAL_SAI_ENABLE_IT() and __HAL_SAI_DISABLE_IT()
  60:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         inside the transmit and receive process.
  61:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  62:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) Make sure that either:
  63:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) PLLSAI1CLK output is configured or
  64:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) PLLSAI2CLK output is configured or
  65:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) PLLSAI3CLK output is configured or
  66:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) External clock source is configured after setting correctly
  67:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****              the define constant EXTERNAL_SAI1_CLOCK_VALUE or EXTERNAL_SAI2_CLOCK_VALUE
  68:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****              in the stm32n6xx_hal_conf.h file.
  69:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  70:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  71:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) In master Tx mode: enabling the audio block immediately generates the bit clock
  72:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         for the external slaves even if there is no data in the FIFO, However FS signal
  73:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         generation is conditioned by the presence of data in the FIFO.
  74:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  75:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  76:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) In master Rx mode: enabling the audio block immediately generates the bit clock
  77:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         and FS signal for the external slaves.
  78:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  79:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  80:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) It is mandatory to respect the following conditions in order to avoid bad SAI behavior:
  81:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) First bit Offset <= (SLOT size - Data size)
  82:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) Data size <= SLOT size
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Antonio\AppData\Local\Temp\ccmFwfsh.s 			page 3


  83:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) Number of SLOT x SLOT size = Frame length
  84:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) The number of slots should be even when SAI_FS_CHANNEL_IDENTIFICATION is selected.
  85:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  86:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  87:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) PDM interface can be activated through HAL_SAI_Init function.
  88:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         Please note that PDM interface is only available for SAI1 sub-block A.
  89:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****         PDM microphone delays can be tuned with HAL_SAIEx_ConfigPdmMicDelay function.
  90:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  91:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  92:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     Three operation modes are available within this driver :
  93:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  94:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     *** Polling mode IO operation ***
  95:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     =================================
  96:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
  97:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Send an amount of data in blocking mode using HAL_SAI_Transmit()
  98:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Receive an amount of data in blocking mode using HAL_SAI_Receive()
  99:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 100:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     *** Interrupt mode IO operation ***
 101:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     ===================================
 102:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 103:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Send an amount of data in non-blocking mode using HAL_SAI_Transmit_IT()
 104:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) At transmission end of transfer HAL_SAI_TxCpltCallback() is executed and user can
 105:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_TxCpltCallback()
 106:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Receive an amount of data in non-blocking mode using HAL_SAI_Receive_IT()
 107:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) At reception end of transfer HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback() is executed and user can
 108:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback()
 109:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) In case of flag error, HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback() function is executed and user can
 110:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback()
 111:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 112:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     *** DMA mode IO operation ***
 113:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     =============================
 114:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 115:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Send an amount of data in non-blocking mode (DMA) using HAL_SAI_Transmit_DMA()
 116:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) At transmission end of transfer HAL_SAI_TxCpltCallback() is executed and user can
 117:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_TxCpltCallback()
 118:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Receive an amount of data in non-blocking mode (DMA) using HAL_SAI_Receive_DMA()
 119:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) At reception end of transfer HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback() is executed and user can
 120:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback()
 121:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) In case of flag error, HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback() function is executed and user can
 122:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback()
 123:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Pause the DMA Transfer using HAL_SAI_DMAPause()
 124:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Resume the DMA Transfer using HAL_SAI_DMAResume()
 125:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Stop the DMA Transfer using HAL_SAI_DMAStop()
 126:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 127:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     *** SAI HAL driver additional function list ***
 128:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     ===============================================
 129:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 130:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       Below the list the others API available SAI HAL driver :
 131:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 132:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) HAL_SAI_EnableTxMuteMode(): Enable the mute in tx mode
 133:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) HAL_SAI_DisableTxMuteMode(): Disable the mute in tx mode
 134:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) HAL_SAI_EnableRxMuteMode(): Enable the mute in Rx mode
